---
import Interior from "../../layouts/Interior.astro";
import MinistryCard from "../../components/MinistryCard.astro";
import {
	families,
	standard,
	counts,
	inHouse,
	familyCount,
	byArea,
	sortEntries,
} from "../../data/ministries";

const signature = sortEntries(inHouse).filter((e) => e.tier === "signature");
const areas = byArea().slice(0, 8);
---

<Interior
	title="Ministries | New Life Grand Rapids"
	description="Signature ministries we run ourselves, and a curated list of the best ministries in Grand Rapids for everything we don't."
	kicker="Signature Ministries & Curated Partnerships"
	heading="Ministries"
	lede="A few things we do well. For everything else, we will tell you who does it best, where they meet, and how to walk in the door."
>
	<!-- The case -->
	<section class="section prose-block">
		<div class="container">
			<p class="eyebrow reveal is-visible">The offering</p>
			<h2 class="prose-block__title reveal is-visible">
				You should not miss out on a ministry because we do not run one.
			</h2>
			<div class="prose-block__body">
				<p class="reveal is-visible">
					Ask most churches what they offer and you get a list of whatever fits inside their
					building. Ours is short. We run {counts.inHouse} ministries here. The list of things a person
					in Grand Rapids might actually be looking for runs to {counts.categories}.
				</p>
				<p class="reveal is-visible">
					That gap is not a confession. It is true of every church in this city, including the
					large ones. A church that tries to do all {counts.categories} does most of them badly, and the
					person who needed the one it did badly is the one who pays for it.
				</p>
				<p class="reveal is-visible">
					So we made a different decision. We are going to be excellent at a few things. For
					everything else, we are going to tell you by name who does it best, where they meet, and
					how to walk in the door.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Two halves -->
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="min-halves reveal is-visible">
				<a class="min-half" href="#signature">
					<span class="min-half__label">In house</span>
					<strong class="min-half__title">Signature Ministries</strong>
					<span class="min-half__count">{counts.inHouse}</span>
					<p>
						What we carry ourselves. Worship, prayer, our kids, our people, and the mission trips we
						have led since 2015.
					</p>
					<span class="min-half__go">See what we run →</span>
				</a>
				<a class="min-half min-half--out" href="#browse">
					<span class="min-half__label">Out of house</span>
					<strong class="min-half__title">Curated Partnerships</strong>
					<span class="min-half__count">{counts.outOfHouse}</span>
					<p>
						Ministries across Grand Rapids that do one thing better than we would. We send people to
						them on purpose.
					</p>
					<span class="min-half__go">Browse all {counts.categories} categories →</span>
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Where the idea came from — Jon's own words -->
	<section class="section prose-block prose-block--tinted">
		<div class="container">
			<p class="eyebrow reveal is-visible">Where this came from</p>
			<h2 class="prose-block__title reveal is-visible">One church leads it. The rest send their people.</h2>
			<div class="prose-block__body">
				<p class="reveal is-visible">
					Years ago, while working out what real collaboration between two churches would look like,
					Jon wrote this down:
				</p>
			</div>
			<blockquote class="min-quote reveal is-visible">
				<p>
					A Ministry Share: Church A leads a ministry and opens it up to the other churches. These
					are ministries that one church takes ownership over and shares with the others. The other
					churches have no obligation to be involved in leading or administering. They can just send
					their people. This is a great opportunity for churches to focus on their strengths and not
					try to do everything.
				</p>
				<cite>Jon Hazeltine, Senior Leader</cite>
			</blockquote>
			<div class="prose-block__body">
				<p class="reveal is-visible">
					This page is that idea pointed outward. Not only the churches sharing our building, but
					every ministry in this city that is genuinely excellent at one thing. If the Body is one,
					then the recovery program on the other side of town is already ours. And yours.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- The curation standard -->
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-heading reveal is-visible">
				<p class="eyebrow">{standard.eyebrow}</p>
				<h2>{standard.title}</h2>
			</div>
			<p class="lead-copy reveal is-visible">{standard.body}</p>
			<div class="min-tests reveal is-visible">
				{standard.tests.map((test, i) => (
					<div class="min-test">
						<span class="min-test__n">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
						<h3>{test.name}</h3>
						<p>{test.body}</p>
					</div>
				))}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- The handoff -->
	<section class="section prose-block prose-block--tinted">
		<div class="container">
			<p class="eyebrow reveal is-visible">The handoff</p>
			<h2 class="prose-block__title reveal is-visible">You get a name, not a link.</h2>
			<div class="prose-block__body">
				<p class="reveal is-visible">
					Referrals usually fail because they end at a website. Someone in the middle of a crisis is
					not going to fill out a contact form at 10 o'clock on a Tuesday night.
				</p>
				<p class="reveal is-visible">
					So every ministry on this list carries a first step written in plain English, and wherever
					we have one, the name of a person who already knows we are sending you. Where we do not
					have that person yet, our job is to go get one. Ask any of our staff to make the
					introduction and they will.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Signature ministries -->
	<section class="section" id="signature">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-heading reveal is-visible">
				<p class="eyebrow">In house</p>
				<h2>What we carry ourselves.</h2>
			</div>
			<p class="lead-copy reveal is-visible">
				These are the ones we would invite the whole city into. Everything we run is listed under
				its category below, alongside the partners.
			</p>
			<div class="min-grid reveal is-visible">
				{signature.map((entry) => <MinistryCard entry={entry} full={true} />)}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Browse by category family -->
	<section class="section" id="browse">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-heading reveal is-visible">
				<p class="eyebrow">The whole map</p>
				<h2>Every category we could think of.</h2>
			</div>
			<p class="lead-copy reveal is-visible">
				{counts.categories} categories in {counts.families} families. Where a number is missing, nobody is on
				that list yet. Those blanks are the work.
			</p>
			<div class="min-families reveal is-visible">
				{families.map((family) => {
					const n = familyCount(family.slug);
					return (
						<a class="min-family" href={`/ministries/${family.slug}`}>
							<div class="min-family__head">
								<h3>{family.name}</h3>
								<span class={n ? "min-family__n" : "min-family__n min-family__n--empty"}>
									{n || "—"}
								</span>
							</div>
							<p>{family.blurb}</p>
							<span class="min-family__cats">
								{family.categories.slice(0, 4).map((c) => c.name).join(" · ")}
								{family.categories.length > 4 && ` · +${family.categories.length - 4} more`}
							</span>
						</a>
					);
				})}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Geography -->
	<section class="section prose-block prose-block--tinted" id="geography">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-heading reveal is-visible">
				<p class="eyebrow">Where they are</p>
				<h2>Close enough to actually go.</h2>
			</div>
			<p class="lead-copy reveal is-visible">
				Practicality decides whether a ministry is real to you. Here is where the curated list sits
				across the area.
			</p>
			<div class="min-areas reveal is-visible">
				{areas.map((group) => (
					<div class="min-area">
						<h3>{group.area}<span>{group.entries.length}</span></h3>
						<ul>
							{group.entries.slice(0, 6).map((entry) => (
								<li><a href={`/ministry/${entry.slug}`}>{entry.name}</a></li>
							))}
							{group.entries.length > 6 && <li class="min-area__more">+{group.entries.length - 6} more</li>}
						</ul>
					</div>
				))}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Honest state -->
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-heading reveal is-visible">
				<p class="eyebrow">Where this stands today</p>
				<h2>Version one, and we are saying so.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose-block__body">
				<p class="reveal is-visible">
					We built the structure first and filled it in from our own knowledge of the city.
					{counts.outOfHouse} ministries are on the list, and not one of them has been confirmed by a
					person at New Life yet. Every card says so until someone here has made the call and had the
					conversation.
				</p>
				<p class="reveal is-visible">
					{counts.uncovered} categories still have nobody in them at all. Those blanks are not an
					oversight. They are the list of conversations we owe the city.
				</p>
				<p class="reveal is-visible">
					If you lead one of these ministries, or you know one we are missing, tell us. This gets
					better by people talking, not by us searching.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="min-cta reveal is-visible">
				<a class="button button--primary" href="https://newlife.ccbchurch.com/goto/forms/156/responses/new">
					Tell us about a ministry
				</a>
				<a class="button button--secondary" href="/unify-gr">About Unify GR</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Interior>
